add('squared-error',['00-01','00-05'],'Turn a prediction into an error','Implement the squared error for a one-weight model y_hat=w*x. Return a scalar; do not take a square root.','double squared_error(double w, double x, double target)','Predict, subtract the target, then square.\n    return 0.0;','    const double residual = w*x-target;\n    return residual*residual;',[
 ('Underprediction','near(squared_error(1,2,6),16)','The residual is -4, so its square is 16.'),('Exact prediction','near(squared_error(3,2,6),0)','A correct prediction has zero error.'),('Overprediction','near(squared_error(4,2,6),4)','Positive and negative residuals both cost error.'),('Negative input','near(squared_error(2,-3,1),49)','Preserve the sign until after subtraction.')],['Compute prediction and residual as separate local variables.','Square the residual, not the prediction.'],'This objective scores one numerical prediction. A language model later uses a different loss, but still separates prediction from evaluation.','Derive the derivative with respect to w without changing the function signature.')
